participant "return_appointments" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Record an appointment no-show
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: POST /api/appointments/:id/actions (NO_SHOW)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Record an appointment no-show
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Check migration 063 schema; require actual participant
Service -> Service: 6: Begin transaction; lock claim context; check request-key replay
Service -> Table: 7: Read appointment and workflow version
activate Table
Table --> Service: 8: Current state, participants and responses
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 9: Check version >0, exact version and non-terminal attempt
alt Action NO_SHOW permitted
Service -> Service: 10: Require ACCEPTED; >=15 minutes past time; both responses PENDING
Service -> Table: 11: Set other participant as no-show; appointment CANCELLED
activate Table
Table --> Service: 12: Updated appointment
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 13: Increase version; write immutable action event
Service -> Service: 14: Persist participant notifications/outboxes; commit
Service --> API: 15: Recorded no-show attempt
API --> Page: 16: HTTP 200: Recorded no-show attempt
Page --> Actor: 17: Show authorized result
else Stale version, invalid actor/state or unsafe context
Service --> API: 10.1: Do not overwrite current appointment
API --> Page: 10.2: HTTP 409
Page --> Actor: 10.3: Display error; do not report success
end
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

